Subject: SUMMARY: using upper tray on PrintServer20 for banner page
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96075316706516

Last Friday after installing PrintServer V4.2 on an Alpha 2100 OSF/1 v3.0
I found that I couldn't use the upper tray for banner pages even after 
uncommenting the documented lines in the sample banner page.  The fix provided
by "Thomas S. Traylor" <TST@swt.edu> is:
----------
What happens is you are resetting Normal-Tray prior to outputing the banner 
page from a different input tray.  Here is what I did to fix bannerPage.psh.

%% 
%% Uncomment the next 3 lines to reset the tray to the original
%  statusdict begin 
%     Normal-Tray setpapertray 
%  end
%%
  % Output the imaged page and force the banner sheet out
  % (in case the printer is set to duplex mode by default).
  %
  showpage
  statusdict begin Normal-Tray setpapertray newsheet end
  } def
----------

I also mentioned that I was no longer able to specify options such as
duplexing and N-up printing using lpr, and that I was annoyed at using
'lpspr | lpr' because this causes the banner page to list the job name
as 'stdin'.  I received several replies from others confirming that the
duplexing and other options are no longer supported directly via lpr.
Suggestions on controlling the job header were to use the -J option to
lpr to explicitly set the job name, or to save the output of lpspr into
a file and then to print that file via lpr.

