From tru64-unix-managers  Tue Jan 17 10:08:24 1995
From: " Andrew T. Lloyd " <atlloyd () acer ! gen ! tcd ! ie>
Date: Tue, 17 Jan 1995 10:08:24 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: LAT tty
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96075316706504

My problem with reallocating /dev/ttys which had been turned
into zombie processes by unclean exits over lat required a
patch:
----------------------------------------------------------------------
/usr/sys/BINARY/kern_exit.o     (CLD UVO102126)
CHECKSUM: 33182    29
---------------------

Patch ID: OSFV30-031-2

In a situation where a streams process on init's child list is hung,
some zombie processes will not get cleaned up from init's child list.
Resources associated with these processes are not available for re-use.
An example is when a user logs out from a LAT terminal, init does not
respawn the 'getty' process, and the LAT line becomes unavailable to
the system (eventually many LAT lines will be unavailable). This
patched version of kern_exit.o corrects the problem.

Kernel rebuild required.
----------------------------------------------------------------------
While I was about it I installed the latopen.o and latclose.o patches
as well following Paul Sand's advice.  Thanks very much to those who
replied (apologies if I've missed anyone):
