Summary:
> We have DEC3000/300 under osf/1 V2.0.
> When we turn the power on, it will automatically boot the system.
> 
> How can we directly get to prompt >>> ?

As the system is powering up, press the "halt" button (on the back of the
case) before it gets fully booted.  This will give you the ">>>" prompt
without having to fully load the OS and then issue a "halt" or "shutdown -h"
from the root account.

If you want the default action on power up to be to halt in the console,
issue the SET AUTO_ACTION HALT command.  Use the SHOW command first to see
how it's currently set.

> Also how do we boot to single user mode from >>>
> I tried b/2, but didn't work.

At the ">>>" prompt, issue the "boot -fl s" command.  Flag "s" (or "S")
means come up to single-user mode.

Benlu Jiang

