I had problems with getting the X server to start up with my customized
kernel (made by doconfig) - while the genvmunix kernel worked fine.

Turns out that I had to include a controller vga line in my configuration
file. After including the entry

controller      vga0       at * slot ? vector vgaintr

and doing another doconfig, the X server starts up with my customized kernel
too. Thanks to DEC CSC Norway for pointing this out. I don't know why it
wasn't found by default, but I don't care as long as it works now.

