X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96075316706551

I doubt this has anything to do with your problem, but you should never modify
/sbin/rc3.d on an OSF box.  You should create a file in rc3.d named e.g.
S89arclmgr, and it will be executed by rc3 automatically.  The convention
for file names in that directory is that they start with a capital "S"
followed by a two digit sequence number followed by the name of the thing
they start.

- Brad

